.TH TPLOT 1.SH NAMEtplot \- plot data on an Atari ST screen.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtplot\fR[\-a=file] [\-x=title] [\-y=title] [\-t=title] [file ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBtplot\fRplots points read from the files named, or from the standard input: twonumbers to a line, x then y, and a blank line lifts the pen.  It asksfor the axes first -- the x interval, the y interval and the x and ydivisions, two numbers to each answer -- unless\fB\-a\fRnames a file holding those three lines.  It calls itself\fBhiplot\fRin its usage line..PPIt draws with the Atari ST's line-A graphics calls, so it needs an OS-9Atari ST to plot on.  At a character terminal it asks its threequestions and then stops where the drawing would begin..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-a=\fIfile\fRtake the three axis answers from\fIfile\fRinstead of asking..TP 12\fB\-x=\fItitle\fR.TP 12\fB\-y=\fItitle\fR.TP 12\fB\-t=\fItitle\fRtitles for the x axis, the y axis and the plot..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOgraph, gnuplot